do
    local category = ccb.content.SnippetCategory { id = "<serum_testing_learning>" }
    category:entry {
        id = "serum_testing_learning_1",
        text = ccb.content.text("Inject subject with 10 ml of 7x-\"Lore\" compound\nSubject was provided with a set of reference textbooks and the latest version of the ACT test (sans writing section) and instructed to complete it as quickly as possible while freely referencing the provided textbooks.  Despite having to occasionally reference the textbooks, subject completed each section in full before the allotted time expired (English in 27 minutes, 12 seconds; math in 40 minutes, 4 seconds; reading in 33 minutes, 56 seconds; and science in 32 minutes, 1 second).  The final score was 27, in the 88th percentile (admittedly, of high school students).\nDuring the testing period, researchers carefully observed the subject's behavior, particularly for any evidence of fidgeting or loss of concentration.  Fidgeting was observed within normal parameters (e.g. drumming fingers on table while thinking), but the subject did not lose concentration or cease working on the test for longer than ten seconds during any testing section.\nFollowing the ACT test administration, the subject was immediately given a series of logic puzzles to complete, and did so without taking a break or losing concentration.\nFollowing expiration of compound, subject reported to infirmary two hours after experiment ended, complaining of severe eye pain following a walk outside.  Further research necessary to counteract photosensitive effects."),
    }
    ccb.content.add(category)
end

do
    local category = ccb.content.SnippetCategory { id = "<serum_testing_speed>" }
    category:entry {
        id = "serum_testing_speed_1",
        text = ccb.content.text("Inject subject with 10 ml of 51x-\"Landru\" compound\nSubject was first asked to run distances of 100m, 400m, and 1 km; times were compared to previously-set reference times taken the previous day.  While the subject measureably improved their performance, finishing an average of 7% faster, the difference was still within normative athletic performance for subject's age and sex.\nFollowing period of rest, subject was asked to perform a target-shooting demonstration using a standard-issue sidearm at 50m and completed it less than ten seconds.  Observers at the time stated the that the subject barely appeared to aim at all; playback of recorded video shows subject making extremely-rapid small adjustments to aim at a greatly-increased speed.\nFollowing demonstration, subject was leaving the room when they accidentally struck the table with their knee.  They collapsed on the ground, grabbing their knee, but a subsequent examination showed no serious or lasting injury.  Subject would only say that it, \"hurt like absolute hell\" and refused further treatment.\nOver the course of the observation period, subject ate approximately 25% more food than normal without an appreciable gain in body mass (measured at the beginning and end of the week-long period).  Recipients of 51x-\"Landru\" should be sure to follow proper dietary protocols."),
    }
    ccb.content.add(category)
end

do
    local category = ccb.content.SnippetCategory { id = "<serum_testing_night_ops>" }
    category:entry {
        id = "serum_testing_night_ops_1",
        text = ccb.content.text("Inject subject with 10 ml of 09x-\"Anaximander\" compound\nSubject was provided with a standard glowstick and ordered to navigate a three-dimensional maze.  Subject found the exit in three minutes and ten seconds, compared to control who found the exit in ten minutes and forty-five seconds (lacking effective amnestics, we cannot test the subject both with and without Anaximander in the same maze).\nSubject was released into the forest nearby and given a ten minute headstart before a team of five trained search-and-rescue personnel were dispatched to locate them.  Subject remained undetected for the full fifteen minutes of the trial and was only found when they returned to base.  When asked how they had evaded the searchers, the subject was unable to answer.  Further testing indicated that the subject had completely lost their voice.\nSubject was asked to walk a mile through the woods to a predetermined point, reaching it in twenty-five minutes.  When asked to write down the reason for the slower time, the subject indicated that they had stopped to take frequent rest breaks due to fatigue.\nWhen the serum wore off after approximately nine hours, the subject reported great sensitivity to light, as well as that they had \"sweated like a pig in heat.\"  They underwent a full medical examination the next day, which showed no lasting ill effects."),
    }
    ccb.content.add(category)
end

